<p>This week introduces the discipline of physics and its relevance to everyday life. We survey the major branches of physics and then dive into <strong>kinematics</strong> — the mathematical description of motion. You will learn how to describe position, velocity, and acceleration quantitatively, use the kinematic equations for constant acceleration, and apply these tools to free-fall problems and motion graphs.</p>

